<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calvinism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Calvinist</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Calvinism is a branch of Protestant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> based on the teachings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-calvin">John Calvin</a>, a sixteenth-century reformer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>. It spread across parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, where it was recognised legally only in 1648 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> it found adherents among the nobility, protected by the Commonwealth's policy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/religious-tolerance">religious tolerance</a>.</p></div>
